Package: cinspecies
Title: Climate Intelligence for Niche Simulation of Forest and Grassland Plant Species
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: person("Mateus", "dos Santos Neves", , "mateus.santos@ufpr.br", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Automated workflow for ecological niche and species distribution
    modelling of terrestrial plants - trees, shrubs, natural-grassland species,
    lianas and epiphytes - that couples ensemble models with land use and land
    cover to map realized habitat at 30 m. Records are retrieved from GBIF
    through 'rgbif' and filtered for plants (cultivated and planted records,
    fossils, uncertain coordinates), cleaned with 'CoordinateCleaner'
    (Zizka et al. 2019 <doi:10.1111/2041-210X.13152>) and thinned with 'spThin'
    (Aiello-Lammens et al. 2015 <doi:10.1111/ecog.01132>). The calibration area
    (M) can be derived automatically (Barve et al. 2011
    <doi:10.1016/j.ecolmodel.2011.02.011>). Predictors are WorldClim 2.1
    (Fick and Hijmans 2017 <doi:10.1002/joc.5086>), optional SoilGrids and
    topography, filtered by VIF with 'usdm'. Models are fitted and
    ensembled with 'sdm' (Naimi and Araujo 2016 <doi:10.1111/ecog.01881>),
    binarised at the maximum TSS threshold (Liu et al. 2013
    <doi:10.1111/jbi.12058>), combined with MapBiomas (Souza et al. 2020
    <doi:10.3390/rs12172735>) or ESA WorldCover habitat chosen by life form,
    projected to CMIP6 futures (Eyring et al. 2016
    <doi:10.5194/gmd-9-1937-2016>) averaged across GCMs, and summarised in
    geodetic area reports of potential and realized habitat.
